# /etc/chrony/sources.d/oci.sources
# OCI's link-local NTP service. Ubuntu's chrony.conf already reads sourcedir
# /etc/chrony/sources.d and keeps "makestep 1 3": the clock may be STEPPED only
# in the first three updates after boot (before the recorders start, see
# time-sync.target + chrony-wait.service); afterwards it is only SLEWED, which
# moves CLOCK_REALTIME and CLOCK_MONOTONIC together and so never trips the
# recorder's 2 s wall-versus-monotonic discontinuity rule.
server 169.254.169.254 iburst
